From: fish <lunarisfelix02@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] op7t-0220: privileges granted by entitlement, as AMFI does (Safari's 30 s first page)

Safari showed its first page only ~25-30 s after launch. Spindump during
the wait: MobileSafari, WebContent, GPU and Networking processes all idle,
no request in flight. oslog: MobileSafari "-[WKWebView _didCommitLayerTree:]
- finally received commit 30.44s after visible content rect update
request", and every 3 s the kernel: "necp_application_find_policy_match_
internal: com.apple.WebKit(..) does not hold the necessary entitlement to
delegate network traffic for other processes". The Networking binary IS
entitled (com.apple.private.network.socket-delegate), but priv_check_cred
-> mac_priv_grant only had sweet_amfi.c's hook, which granted
PRIV_WORK_INTERVAL and nothing else.

Now the hook grants a privilege when the calling process's signature
carries the matching entitlement. The table holds the names read from the
denied processes' own entitlements (SpringBoard, dasd, aggregated,
symptomsd, nsurlsessiond, mDNSResponder, mediaserverd, WebKit Networking):
global-proc-info, system-override, selective-forced-idle, darkboot,
audio_latency, override-cpumon, socket-delegate, interface-control,
network statistics, NECP policies/match, AWDL, IPsec wake packet, reserved
port, Skywalk user pipe / net_if / observe. Others stay denied and logged.

Apply after 0219.
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
--- a/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c
@@ -602,12 +602,52 @@ static struct {
 } sweet_priv_logged[SWEET_PRIV_LOG_MAX];
 static int sweet_priv_logged_count;
 
+/*
+ * 0220: as AMFI does, a privilege is granted when the process's code signature carries the entitlement for it.
+ * Names read from the entitlements of the processes that were denied (ldid -e on the phone, 2026-11-13): e.g.
+ * WebKit's Networking process was refused PRIV_NET_PRIVILEGED_SOCKET_DELEGATE although it is entitled, NECP
+ * retried every 3 s and Safari's first page took ~30 s ("finally received commit 30.44s after ..."). Privileges
+ * not listed here stay denied (and logged once per process).
+ */
+static const struct {
+	int priv;
+	const char *entitlement;
+} sweet_priv_entitlements[] = {
+	{ PRIV_GLOBAL_PROC_INFO, "com.apple.private.kernel.global-proc-info" },
+	{ PRIV_SYSTEM_OVERRIDE, "com.apple.private.kernel.system-override" },
+	{ PRIV_SELECTIVE_FORCED_IDLE, "com.apple.private.kernel.selective-forced-idle" },
+	{ PRIV_DARKBOOT, "com.apple.private.kernel.darkboot" },
+	{ PRIV_AUDIO_LATENCY, "com.apple.private.kernel.audio_latency" },
+	{ PRIV_PROC_CPUMON_OVERRIDE, "com.apple.private.kernel.override-cpumon" },
+	{ PRIV_NET_PRIVILEGED_SOCKET_DELEGATE, "com.apple.private.network.socket-delegate" },
+	{ PRIV_NET_INTERFACE_CONTROL, "com.apple.private.network.interface-control" },
+	{ PRIV_NET_PRIVILEGED_NETWORK_STATISTICS, "com.apple.private.network.statistics" },
+	{ PRIV_NET_PRIVILEGED_NECP_POLICIES, "com.apple.private.necp.policies" },
+	{ PRIV_NET_RESTRICTED_AWDL, "com.apple.private.network.awdl.restricted" },
+	{ PRIV_NET_PRIVILEGED_NECP_MATCH, "com.apple.private.necp.match" },
+	{ PRIV_NET_PRIVILEGED_IPSEC_WAKE_PACKET, "com.apple.private.network.ipsec-wake-packet" },
+	{ PRIV_NETINET_RESERVEDPORT, "com.apple.private.network.reserved-port" },
+	{ PRIV_SKYWALK_REGISTER_USER_PIPE, "com.apple.private.skywalk.register-user-pipe" },
+	{ PRIV_SKYWALK_REGISTER_NET_IF, "com.apple.private.skywalk.register-net-if" },
+	{ PRIV_SKYWALK_OBSERVE_ALL, "com.apple.private.skywalk.observe-all" },
+	{ PRIV_SKYWALK_OBSERVE_STATS, "com.apple.private.skywalk.observe-stats" },
+};
+
 static int
 sweet_sandbox_priv_grant(kauth_cred_t cred __unused, int priv)
 {
 	if (priv == PRIV_WORK_INTERVAL) {
 		return 0;
 	}
+	for (size_t i = 0; i < sizeof(sweet_priv_entitlements) / sizeof(sweet_priv_entitlements[0]); i++) {
+		if (sweet_priv_entitlements[i].priv == priv) {
+			void *ent = sweet_proc_entitlements(current_proc());
+			if (ent != NULL && sweet_entitlements_bool(ent, sweet_priv_entitlements[i].entitlement)) {
+				return 0;
+			}
+			break;
+		}
+	}
 	char name[20];
 	proc_selfname(name, sizeof(name));
 	for (int i = 0; i < sweet_priv_logged_count; i++) {
